                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd490acb-4702-37f1-bbda-b5e9323f7efe",
                        "entry_id": "b6c552bd-681e-3bb8-b585-e57487157e3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A wind blowing across a line of travel, especially perpendicularly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa0a89e6-6e1d-40fd-aa0c-2902e08a487f",
                                "sense_id": "bd490acb-4702-37f1-bbda-b5e9323f7efe",
                                "text": "Correlation of the DFDR and CVR recordings disclosed that the flightcrew had set the flaps and stabilizer trim at 10° and about 5° aircraft noseup, respectively, for takeoff. A rolling takeoff was made, takeoff thrust was stabilized at 80 KIAS, and left rudder and right aileron were used to compensate for the right crosswind. The V₁ and V_R callouts were made about 2 sec after these speeds were recorded by the DFDR."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71314588-f6af-4375-820a-7310323d977a",
                                "sense_id": "bd490acb-4702-37f1-bbda-b5e9323f7efe",
                                "text": "As part of its application, Macy's submitted \"balloon control plans\" describing how handlers, under the direction of a \"pilot,\" were to navigate through intersections, where crosswinds can destabilize the balloons."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4cf01431-2f12-4f7e-a3f0-fd245cb8e5b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6c552bd-681e-3bb8-b585-e57487157e3d",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd490acb-4702-37f1-bbda-b5e9323f7efe",
